Title: Game from a Workbench icon, a file requester, love --icon
Repository: love
Base: def245102c67909f9902095af613b1ae05249b62
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-22
Author: aros-loeve project
Problem: A game could only be started from a Shell. A Workbench start passes a message instead of arguments, which LOVE ignored, so a project icon with LOVE as its default tool showed the no-game screen, and a double click on the program's icon had no way to pick a game. Output of a game started from Workbench opened a console window over the game.
Change: src/aros_start.c: the project of a Workbench start becomes the first argument; a Workbench start without a project asks for the game with an ASL file requester (a .love file, or a drawer with an empty file name; the last drawer is remembered in the variable LOVE.gamedrawer), unless a game is joined to the program file; `love --icon <game>` writes a project icon whose default tool is this program, beside a .love file or on main.lua inside a game drawer (Workbench opens a drawer whatever its icon says), copied from PROGDIR:Game.info; __stdiowin is NIL: so a Workbench start has no console window.
Scope: AROS (all targets)
Upstream: local-only
Verification: mainline x86_64, nightly 2026-11-18, softpipe (pool v1-3), 2026-11-22: `love --icon` on a .love file and on a drawer (second call refused, icon left as it is); WBRun of the .love icon and a mouse double click on the main.lua icon start the game with the game as arg[1]; WBRun of the program opens the requester, a typed drawer starts that game, Cancel gives the no-game screen, the next requester opens in the last drawer; a game icon dropped on the no-game window starts the game. Not run: Raspberry Pi, a program file with a joined game started from Workbench.
Removal: not planned
